    "t7": { "x": 0, "y": 12560, "text": "Pseudo-RTL and the workbench component", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 3920 },
    "q1": { "x": 6040, "y": 1620, "w": 520, "size": "m", "fill": "orange", "text": "Decided here, please confirm:\n• Workbench alone on desktop 1: no gaps and square corners (smart gaps)\n• Top bar 32 px, status bar 24 px, rail 48 px: proposed tokens\n• Pane dividers use --ms-border; in the Muse dark palette that is #858b98, stronger than VS Code's dividers\n• Code renders monochrome because every --ms-syntax-* role resolves to --ms-text\n• Settings and Help sit at the rail's foot without number keys" },
    "q2": { "x": 4120, "y": 3520, "w": 520, "size": "m", "fill": "orange", "text": "At 1280 × 800: chat 340 px, sidebar 232 px, terminal 176 px, minimap 48 px.\nHigh contrast is hc-dark at 1920 and hc-light at 1280, so both high-contrast palettes are drawn. Every sheet's Tweaks switch the theme." },
    "q3": { "x": 8040, "y": 5240, "w": 520, "size": "m", "fill": "orange", "text": "The bar's popovers are drawn side by side for review; only one opens at a time. The numbers tie each popover to its bar item." },
    "q4": { "x": 6040, "y": 7140, "w": 520, "size": "m", "fill": "orange", "text": "The lock screen shows counts only: notifications and running agents, never their content.\nStop everything, Lock admin and Stop machine work without signing in.\nGreeter and lock both say that Ctrl+Alt+Del always shows the real screen (threat model D60)." },
    "q5": { "x": 4040, "y": 9040, "w": 520, "size": "m", "fill": "orange", "text": "The detached terminal joins the tiling here; D91.13 calls a detached terminal floating.\nWindows: --ms-radius-lg corners, --ms-space-4 inner and --ms-space-8 outer gaps, a --ms-focus border at --ms-focus-width on the focused window.\nChrome draws its own interface; it is shown as a neutral frame.\nPack versions and sizes are sample data until TP1's signed index exists." },
    "q6": { "x": 4040, "y": 10940, "w": 520, "size": "m", "fill": "orange", "text": "Device presets use generic names (Phone, Tablet, Laptop, Desktop).\nThe user's app inside the preview is drawn with the light palette as a stand-in for its own CSS." },
    "q7": { "x": 4040, "y": 12840, "w": 520, "size": "m", "fill": "orange", "text": "Pseudo-RTL: UI strings are reversed with a bidi override, in the manner of Android's ar-XB pseudo-locale. File names, code, terminal output and message text stay left to right, and the editor with its minimap stays LTR." }
  },
